  "grammar_explanations": [
    {
      "slug": "there is/there are: affirmative descriptions and questions (Is there ...?)",
      "title_form": "There is / There are: describir lugares y preguntar",
      "title_target": "There is / There are: Describing Places and Asking Questions",
      "description_md_form": "Usamos **there is** para **una** cosa y **there are** para **varias**. Es la forma de decir que algo **existe** en un lugar.\n\n- **There is** + una cosa: `There is a museum.`\n- **There are** + varias cosas: `There are two parks.`\n\nPara preguntar si algo existe, usamos **Is there...?** con una cosa y **Are there...?** con varias:\n\n- `Is there a cafe near here?` (¿Hay un café cerca de aquí?)\n- `Are there any cinemas?` (¿Hay cines?)\n\nEn las respuestas cortas: `Yes, there is.` / `No, there isn't.`",
      "description_md_target": "We use **there is** for **one** thing and **there are** for **several**. It is how we say that something **exists** in a place.\n\n- **There is** + one thing: `There is a museum.`\n- **There are** + several things: `There are two parks.`\n\nTo ask if something exists, we use **Is there...?** with one thing and **Are there...?** with several:\n\n- `Is there a cafe near here?`\n- `Are there any cinemas?`\n\nFor short answers: `Yes, there is.` / `No, there isn't.`",
      "grammar_structure": "There is + singular noun / There are + plural noun / Is there + singular noun + ...?",
      "conjugation_table": {
        "name": "there_is_are",
        "headers": [
          "Forma",
          "Uso",
          "Ejemplo"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "There is",
            "Una cosa",
            "There is a garden."
          ],
          [
            "There are",
            "Varias cosas",
            "There are two cinemas."
          ],
          [
            "Is there...?",
            "Pregunta con una cosa",
            "Is there a bank?"
          ],
          [
            "Are there...?",
            "Pregunta con varias cosas",
            "Are there any hotels?"
          ]
        ]
      },
